        "original_id": "4afc325b-cffc-55ce-8a88-63a7d0eee0e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nick Grinde, Karel Reisz, Hylda Baker, Tony Richardson\n- Works: Saturday Night and Sunday Morning, Nearest and Dearest\n- Places: Britain, Farnworth, Lancashire\n- Topics: British cinema, realist film movement\n\nFacts:\n- Nick Grindé was an American film director and screenwriter who lived from January 12, 1893 to June 19, 1979.\n- Karel Reisz was a British filmmaker who lived from 21 July 1926 to 25 November 2002.\n- Karel Reisz was one of the pioneers of the new realist strain in British cinema during the 1950s and 1960s and was active in post–World War II Britain.\n- Saturday Night and Sunday Morning is a 1960 British drama film directed by Karel Reisz and produced by Tony Richardson.\n- Hylda Baker was born and brought up in Farnworth, Lancashire.\n- Hylda Baker is known for her role in the 1960 film Saturday Night and Sunday Morning.\n- Hylda Baker is perhaps best known for playing Nellie Pledge in the ITV sitcom Nearest and Dearest from 1968 to 1973.",
